    {
      "topic": "certificate",
      "finding": "The schema requires certified=true independent bounds plus method, source and physical traceability, not a named accreditation or formal CoA file. A defensible independently assayed physical blank can support an operational negative; it must meet the declared evidence semantics. Do not relabel a point estimate, nominal zero, or purity marketing claim as certified upper bound."
    },
    {
      "topic": "instrument",
      "finding": "Current software binds ChemCam LANL exactly. Cross-instrument evaluation of unchanged weights is scientifically possible as explicitly OOD validation, but needs a separately reviewed versioned protocol/adapter contract before opening scores. It cannot pass the current contract by renaming the instrument; retraining is not inherently necessary for OOD testing and would change the frozen model."
    },
    {
      "topic": "support",
      "finding": "No fixed 30/59/73-material requirement has been frozen. Declare estimand and precision first. Shot repeats and same family/session do not create independent clusters."
    },
    {
      "topic": "blank",
      "finding": "Fe and Mg may use different documented method/matrix blank families. A low positive assay point can support an ordinary operational negative but cannot alone establish blank upper-bound evidence. Dark/no-laser files are not method/matrix blanks."
    }
